            <ArticleTitle>Induced Membrane Technique: Pearls and Pitfalls.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>S36-S38</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/BOT.0000000000000979</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The induced membrane technique for reconstruction of bone defects has proved its effectiveness and is now widely accepted. The 2 stages procedure, implying a cement spacer in the first stage and a huge bone graft in the second stage, responds to rigorous technical details involving each phase of the procedure. Prerequisites for the technique, cement spacer, bone fixation, time between the 2 stages, grafting, and postoperative course are reported and discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
